{
 "_note": "Stand-in home pages for the guided start's style previews (AGL-3898), one per AI_SITE_KINDS id, each in its own kind's shape (a gallery for photography, a menu for a café, a product grid for a store, a reading list for a blog, dates for events, listings for real estate, a class schedule for yoga), in the layout language a site job's page step answers in (ai-layout-language.ts). Written by hand, never by a model: render-site-style-previews.mts compiles each through compile-recorded-sites.mts (the real page check and compiler, the kind's design variants, the look the kind's look unit builds) and shoots it. `hero` is the kind's signature hero (aiLayoutKindSignature's first, AGL-3985), which the seed is chosen for with any `choices` (other design variants) and `look` (the header's arrangement); `opensOnGrid` marks a page whose first section is a grid of pictures, drawn as written. `photos` fills each picture slot in order with a starter photo's key (hero, about, desk, plants, craft), a `{ photo, crop: [left, top, width, height], alt }` part of one, or a `{ file, crop?, alt }` preview photo of the kind's own business from style-preview-photos/ (credited in its CREDITS.md, never a site's starter); every page opens on one, since a band of type with no photo reads as a picture that failed to load (AGL-3985). `nav` names the site's other pages, which the header links, and `cta` the header's button, which goes to the last of them or to `ctaTo`; a section's `items` says how many records it lists where its blocks carry none (a blog's posts); `products` are a store's records, `posts` a blog's, and `facts` what the brief says beside the kind (a time or a date the page shows must be in it).",
